@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "customer.integration"

Feature:  Koroneiki to Customer Employee Integration
	Testing to assure that koroneiki employee information transfers properly to customer.

Teardown:
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| ${staticEmailValue1} |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| ${staticEmailValue1} |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| ${staticEmailValue1} |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| ${staticEmailValue1} |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| ${staticEmailValue1} |

Scenario: View Liferay employee
	New Liferay employees who are added to koroneiki via okta should sync correctly to Customer

	Given I generate static variables for support user
	And I rename the first support user variables
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | ${staticScreenNameValue1}       |
	| Email Address | ${staticEmailValue1}            |
	| First Name    | ${staticContactFirstNameValue1} |
	| Last Name     | ${staticContactLastNameValue1}  |
	| Group         | Employees                       |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "${staticEmailValue1}" added via automatic sync
	And the account with the name "Liferay, Inc." should be assigned the contact with the email address "${staticEmailValue1}" via automatic sync
	When I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Employee"
	Then the support user with the email address "${staticEmailValue1}" should be synced to the support site
	And the support user with the email address "${staticEmailValue1}" should be part of the support organization with the name "Employees"
	And the support user with the email address "${staticEmailValue1}" should be part of the support organization with the name "Koroneiki Customer"
	And the support user with the email address "${staticEmailValue1}" should be part of the support organization with the name "Koroneiki Customer - DXP"
	And the support user with the email address "${staticEmailValue1}" should be part of the support organization with the name "Koroneiki Customer - Portal"
	And the support user with the email address "${staticEmailValue1}" should be part of the support organization with the name "Koroneiki Customer - Commerce"
	And I log into the customer homepage as "${staticCustomerAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticCustomerAdminPassword}"